                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Disclaimer:\nThis review is based on my personal experience, YMMV.\nIf you are sensitive to loud sounds like me you may not enjoy it very much.\n\nWhen I first started the game I got slapped in the ears with obnoxiously loud, repetitive and annoying music which you can not turn off. You can not adjust volume. It keeps repeating the few bars ad nauseam while you desperately try to fight the stunning and disorienting effect of your ears assaulted by the painfully loud audio just to play the game. When I entered the tutorial I heard a crackling, barely comprehensible 2 kHz quality sample repeating \"Please click on the arrow\" over and over when I followed the prompts and fumbled through the awkward controls. Thankfully the \"please click on the arrow\" seems to be the only spoken phrase in the game, I am not sure if I could have taken any more of that.\n\nThe options menu has one option: Chinese or English.\nYes, that's it. Chinese or English.\n\nI am quite convinced that if Hell existed this would be one of the games I would have to play for all eternity...\n\nAfter unplugging my headset from my Vive) was a pretty simple tower defense game in VR which might appeal to some people The controls were a bit iffu but with practise you might be able to control the turrets better. The bow on the archery tower was placed outside my play area, which made it almost impossible to use because it was inside the real physical wall in my room.\n\nBut I think the initial impression was enough for me. At least it was cheap because I got it as a part of Humble Bundle.",
